{"title":"Career Roadmap: NGO Project Coordinator","role":"NGO Project Coordinator","summary":"An NGO Project Coordinator supports the planning, implementation, monitoring and reporting of development projects.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours)","Course":"Rural Development / Women's Studies / Gender Studies"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build skills in development programmes, project coordination, community engagement, budgeting, monitoring & evaluation, documentation and stakeholder management"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An NGO Project Coordinator supports the planning, implementation, monitoring and reporting of development projects."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Project planning"},{"text":"Community coordination"},{"text":"Field-team coordination"},{"text":"Beneficiary engagement"},{"text":"Activity scheduling"},{"text":"Partner coordination"},{"text":"Budget tracking"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Monitoring & evaluation"},{"text":"Donor reporting"},{"text":"Government coordination"},{"text":"Volunteer management"},{"text":"Risk management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The specialization is particularly relevant for programmes involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rural development"},{"text":"Women's empowerment"},{"text":"Gender equality"},{"text":"Livelihoods"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Public health"},{"text":"Child development"},{"text":"Skill development"},{"text":"Financial inclusion"},{"text":"Community development"},{"text":"Social protection"},{"text":"CSR and social-impact programmes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A graduate will often enter as a Project Assistant, Programme Associate, Field Coordinator or Programme Coordinator before progressing into a full Project Coordinator role."}]},{"heading":"What to Build Duri